## Recovery — honest table

| Failure mode | What recovers it |
|---|---|
| Idle at context limit (session full, account has capacity) | a cron **inside that lane's own session** works |
| Wedged tooling | **nothing automated** — needs a NEW session |
| Usage limit (account capacity exhausted) | **nothing automated** — a cron spends the capacity the limit removed; time resets it |
| Full session crash / process death | **nothing automated** — the cron died with the session |

**Recovery is the owner re-pasting `runs/run-{NN}/prompts/PROMPT-<X>.md`.** That is why the
prompts are files and not chat scrollback. No planner-registered crons exist in this run.

